      "text": "6/6 — What can India learn? 🇮🇳\n\nDespite my criticism, I genuinely appreciate Tesla’s innovation.\n\nI think Indian automobile companies like Tata and Mahindra should invest even more in experimental technologies, advanced batteries, software and original R&D.\n\nNot every innovation needs to be commercially successful immediately. Sometimes, experimenting is how breakthroughs happen.\n\nIndia has the engineers, talent and market.\n\nWe shouldn’t just focus on manufacturing the cars of tomorrow. We should also work on inventing them.",
